.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt EGGHEAD 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm config.yml
.Nd egghead configuration file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa ~/.config/egghead/config.yml
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm egghead
reads its configuration from a single YAML file. With no
configuration file and no environment variables set, the system
still comes up: record reading, search, the TUI records browser, and
the eight record-related MCP tools all work. Anything that needs an
LLM returns an error in that mode.
.Pp
The file location is resolved in this order, taking the first match:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Ev EGGHEAD_CONFIG ,
if set. May point at a directory (in which case
.Pa config.yml
inside it is read) or directly at a YAML file.
.It
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/egghead/config.yml ,
when the variable is set.
.It
.Pa ~/.config/egghead/config.yml
otherwise.
.El
.Pp
.Cm egghead config path
prints the resolved path. When
.Nm egghead
writes the file, it sets the file mode to
.Sy 0600
on the assumption that API keys may end up inside.
.Pp
Three layers determine an effective setting; the highest layer
that has a value wins:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
Environment variables. Provider API keys
.Pq Ev ANTHROPIC_API_KEY , Ev OPENAI_API_KEY , and so on
are detected at startup and override anything in the configuration
file.
.It
The configuration file.
.It
Built-in defaults.
.El
.Pp
The practical implication: the configuration file is for persistent,
considered choices; the environment is for credentials and
per-session overrides.
.Sh KEYS
Every key is optional. A configuration file containing only
.Sy default_model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
is a legal file.
.Bl -tag -width "default_model"
.It Sy records_dir
Where records live. Tilde expansion is honored. Default:
.Pa ~/.egghead .
.It Sy skills_dir
Drop-zone for portable skills outside the records directory. Default:
.Pa ~/.agents/skills .
.It Sy sandbox
Workspace ceiling for
.Sy fs.*
and
.Sy proc.*
grants. Optional; can be declared per-agent instead.
.It Sy llm
List of LLM providers. Each entry has a
.Sy provider:
(one of
.Sy anthropic ,
.Sy openai ,
.Sy google ,
.Sy xai ,
.Sy groq ,
.Sy deepseek ,
.Sy mistral ,
.Sy openrouter ,
.Sy ollama ,
.Sy lmstudio ,
or a custom OpenAI-compatible name) and an
.Sy api_key:
.Pq literal or Sy {env:VAR} .
Optional
.Sy name:
distinguishes a custom entry from a default of the same provider;
optional
.Sy base_url:
opts into an OpenAI-compatible endpoint other than the provider's
own.
.It Sy default_model
Model in
.Sy provider/model
form, used for new agents and 1:1 prompts. Default:
.Sy anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6 .
.It Sy default_room
Default chat-room id, created on demand. Default:
.Sy default .
.It Sy web.port
TCP port the web server listens on. Default:
.Sy 4000 .
.It Sy web.host
Host used in generated absolute URLs. Default:
.Sy localhost .
.It Sy web.bind
Listen address. Default:
.Sy 127.0.0.1 .
Set to
.Sy 0.0.0.0
to bind every interface; only safe behind a reverse proxy or on a
network that authenticates connections itself
.Pq tailnet, private VPC .
.It Sy server.host
Hostname this node registers under for cross-host BEAM distribution.
Switches the BEAM to longnames. Required for cross-host attach;
omit it for same-host attach (which is zero-config).
.It Sy server.port_range
Inclusive
.Sy [min, max]
range pinning the BEAM distribution listener's port range, so a
single firewall rule covers it.
.It Sy mcp_servers
List of external MCP servers
.Nm egghead
mounts as a client. Each entry has a
.Sy name: ,
a
.Sy transport:
.Pq Sy stdio No or Sy http ,
either a
.Sy command:
or a
.Sy url: ,
optional
.Sy env: ,
and a
.Sy requires:
list naming the capabilities an agent must already hold to be offered
this server's tools. The
.Sy requires:
grammar matches
.Sy capabilities:
on agent records.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT REFERENCES
Anywhere a string value could be sensitive, write
.Sy {env:VAR}
and
.Nm egghead
resolves it from the environment at load time. The literal string
sits in the file; the secret stays in the environment. This pattern
lets you commit the configuration file under version control without
committing the keys.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
llm:
  - provider: anthropic
    api_key: "{env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}"
.Ed
.Sh AUTO-DETECTED PROVIDERS
If the
.Sy llm:
section is empty (or the configuration file does not exist at all),
.Nm egghead
checks for these environment variables at startup and registers the
corresponding providers automatically:
.Bl -column -compact "openrouter " "GOOGLE_API_KEY or GEMINI_API_KEY"
.It Sy anthropic   Ta Ev ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
.It Sy openai      Ta Ev OPENAI_API_KEY
.It Sy google      Ta Ev GOOGLE_API_KEY No or Ev GEMINI_API_KEY
.It Sy xai         Ta Ev XAI_API_KEY
.It Sy groq        Ta Ev GROQ_API_KEY
.It Sy deepseek    Ta Ev DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
.It Sy mistral     Ta Ev MISTRAL_API_KEY
.It Sy openrouter  Ta Ev OPENROUTER_API_KEY
.El
.Sh EXAMPLE
.Bd -literal -offset indent
records_dir: ~/.egghead

llm:
  - provider: anthropic
    api_key: "{env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}"

  - provider: openai
    name: together
    base_url: https://api.together.xyz/v1
    api_key: "{env:TOGETHER_API_KEY}"

default_model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6

web:
  port: 4000
  host: localhost
  bind: 127.0.0.1

# Optional — only needed for cross-host BEAM distribution.
server:
  host: orca.tailnet.ts.net
  port_range: [9100, 9105]

mcp_servers:
  - name: exa
    transport: stdio
    command: npx -y exa-mcp-server
    env:
      EXA_API_KEY: "{env:EXA_API_KEY}"
    requires:
      - net.get:
          hosts: ["api.exa.ai"]
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.local/state/egghead/egghead.log"
.It Pa ~/.config/egghead/config.yml
The configuration file.
.It Pa ~/.egghead/
Default records directory.
.It Pa ~/.egghead/.egghead/index.db
Derived SQLite index, rebuilt from records on demand.
.It Pa ~/.local/state/egghead/egghead.log
Application log file.
.It Pa ~/.erlang.cookie
BEAM distribution cookie. Required at the same path on every host
participating in cross-host attach.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr egghead 1 ,
.Xr egghead-init 1 ,
.Xr egghead-config 1 ,
.Xr egghead-llm 1 ,
.Xr egghead 7
